WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.803
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.103 --> 00:00:09.396
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.696 --> 00:00:15.321
Unit thirteen: Cause and Effect. Today you will explain causes and results with clear language.

4
00:00:15.621 --> 00:00:18.215
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:22.492
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:24.212
Cause.

7
00:00:25.217 --> 00:00:27.553
Cause means the reason something happens.

8
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.778
Pollution is a cause.

9
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:33.012
Your turn. Say: Cause.

10
00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:36.937
Cause.

11
00:00:37.683 --> 00:00:38.638
Effect.

12
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.359
Effect means a result.

13
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.624
The effect was serious.

14
00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:46.881
Your turn. Say: Effect.

15
00:00:49.733 --> 00:00:50.688
Effect.

16
00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:52.463
Result in.

17
00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.403
Result in means to lead to.

18
00:00:56.017 --> 00:00:57.981
Smoking results in illness.

19
00:00:58.583 --> 00:01:01.874
Your turn. Say: Result in.

20
00:01:04.733 --> 00:01:05.967
Result in.

21
00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:07.509
Due to.

22
00:01:08.517 --> 00:01:09.994
Due to means because of.

23
00:01:10.583 --> 00:01:12.200
Due to rain, we stayed.

24
00:01:12.783 --> 00:01:14.983
Your turn. Say: Due to.

25
00:01:17.833 --> 00:01:18.672
Due to.

26
00:01:19.417 --> 00:01:20.325
Therefore.

27
00:01:21.317 --> 00:01:23.235
Therefore means as a result.

28
00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.687
Therefore, prices rose.

29
00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:28.587
Your turn. Say: Therefore.

30
00:01:31.433 --> 00:01:32.388
Therefore.

31
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.139
Contribute.

32
00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.138
Contribute means to help cause.

33
00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.552
Cars contribute to smog.

34
00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:42.663
Your turn. Say: Contribute.

35
00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:46.606
Contribute.

36
00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:48.281
Lead to.

37
00:01:49.283 --> 00:01:50.900
Lead to means to cause.

38
00:01:51.483 --> 00:01:53.204
Stress can lead to illness.

39
00:01:53.817 --> 00:01:56.411
Your turn. Say: Lead to.

40
00:01:59.267 --> 00:02:00.326
Lead to.

41
00:02:01.083 --> 00:02:02.259
Consequence.

42
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:05.760
Consequence means a result of an action.

43
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.059
Think of the consequences.

44
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:11.221
Your turn. Say: Consequence.

45
00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.277
Consequence.

46
00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:20.043
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.883 --> 00:02:23.858
Visal, how do I explain cause and effect?

48
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:32.804
Use structures such as because of, due to, leads to and results in. For example, heavy traffic leads to air pollution.

49
00:02:33.917 --> 00:02:35.905
Which linking words show result?

50
00:02:37.017 --> 00:02:47.320
Use therefore, as a result and consequently at the start of a sentence, followed by a comma. They link a cause in one sentence to its effect in the next.

51
00:02:48.417 --> 00:02:49.731
Is one cause enough?

52
00:02:50.817 --> 00:03:02.385
Often there are several causes. Use contribute to or one factor to show that a result has more than one cause, and avoid saying that something is the only reason.

53
00:03:03.533 --> 00:03:05.045
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:05.883 --> 00:03:09.172
Grammar focus: Linking cause and result.

55
00:03:09.472 --> 00:03:10.612
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:11.317 --> 00:03:13.665
Heavy traffic leads to air pollution.

57
00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:18.294
Prices rose. As a result, fewer people bought cars.

58
00:03:19.233 --> 00:03:25.659
Use because of, due to and as a result of plus a noun phrase. Use because, so and therefore with a clause.

59
00:03:26.417 --> 00:03:29.580
Be careful! Don't say: Rain lead to flood.

60
00:03:31.533 --> 00:03:33.753
Say: Rain leads to floods.

61
00:03:34.053 --> 00:03:36.018
Add s and use a plural noun.

62
00:03:36.833 --> 00:03:39.416
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.410
Why Did It Happen?.

64
00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:44.546
Sambath studies a report on air pollution.

65
00:03:45.533 --> 00:03:48.253
Heavy traffic is one major cause of the problem.

66
00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:51.731
It leads to health problems such as asthma.

67
00:03:52.733 --> 00:03:55.731
As a result, the city introduces cycle lanes.

68
00:03:56.733 --> 00:03:59.290
The consequence is cleaner air in the centre.

69
00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.135
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:04.983 --> 00:04:06.344
A cause is a blank.

71
00:04:06.644 --> 00:04:10.240
A, title. B, reason. C, picture.

72
00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.498
The answer is B: reason.

73
00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:18.417
Therefore means as a blank.

74
00:04:18.717 --> 00:04:21.825
A, rule. B, rest. C, result.

75
00:04:25.367 --> 00:04:27.262
The answer is C: result.

76
00:04:28.417 --> 00:04:29.929
Leads to means blank.

77
00:04:30.229 --> 00:04:34.091
A, causes. B, avoids. C, ends.

78
00:04:37.633 --> 00:04:39.598
The answer is A: causes.

79
00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.750
Due to is followed by a blank.

80
00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:46.680
A, number only. B, noun phrase. C, question.

81
00:04:50.233 --> 00:04:52.419
The answer is B: noun phrase.

82
00:04:53.583 --> 00:04:55.455
What did the city introduce?

83
00:04:55.755 --> 00:04:59.989
A, a tax. B, a stadium. C, cycle lanes.

84
00:05:03.533 --> 00:05:05.614
The answer is C: cycle lanes.

85
00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:09.998
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:13.012
How do you explain cause and effect?

87
00:05:21.817 --> 00:05:23.363
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:23.663 --> 00:05:34.631
I use phrases such as because of, leads to and results in. I also use linking words such as therefore and as a result. I remember that a problem often has several causes.

89
00:05:34.931 --> 00:05:36.687
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:37.583 --> 00:05:42.082
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and linking cause and result.

91
00:05:42.382 --> 00:05:46.868
Today's value is critical reasoning. Test every argument before you accept it.

92
00:05:47.168 --> 00:05:50.088
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:50.388 --> 00:05:53.365
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

